{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles","id":1530389,"title":"Future WoD5 Titles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-09T10:01:10-08:00","id":1530389,"title":"Future WoD5 Titles?","content":"Hoo boy, I'm opening a can of worms with this topic but I'm going to be as civil as possible with this topic. I strongly encourage that anyone who posts here also keeps it civil. This is meant to be a containment thread for further future Parawolf X5 discussion.<br /> <br /> As a quick disclaimer, I personally hate all of the 5th Editions of the WoD games so far, but Parawolf is dead set on pushing it and will likely do so for the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> There's rumors that the pre-V5 setting will be brought back and re-supported under the banner of &quot;Legacy World of Darkness&quot; with the WoD5 material being treated as a soft reboot/alternate continuity of sorts, but these are just rumors for the time being as far as I can tell and I'll believe it when I see it.<br /> <br /> With that said, let's try to speculate what potential 5th Editions of Mage, Wraith, Changeling, Mummy, and Demon will be like....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-09-2024, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T10:54:34-08:00","id":1530390,"title":"","content":"Let's not. We've had this a couple of times already and it's just a good way to get people's bile up. Let it go, it will be what it will be. Vote with your waller and play what you enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T12:05:10-08:00","id":1530393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530390#post1530390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not. We've had this a couple of times already and it's just a good way to get people's bile up. Let it go, it will be what it will be. Vote with your waller and play what you enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree completely and I'm never going to be paying money for any Parawolf X5 stuff.<br /> <br /> But I figured it'd be best to create a containment thread for all of the speculation/discussion and keep it in one place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T13:33:23-08:00","id":1530400,"title":"","content":"I made another treat like that, but no much sucess.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was wondering what it would be like to make V5 versions of Demon the Fallen and Mummy the Resurrection and I really wonder if it would change a lot, mechanically maybe DtF would be more simplified and they might want to say that they are Nephilim instead of Fallen. The mummies, I don't know to what extent they could use this plot, I don't think it would change that much mechanically, but I don't know what the vibe would be like, unless they decided to use MtC as a reference.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T14:44:17-08:00","id":1530403,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I doubt we'll see an X5 version of Mummy: The Resurrection. MTR was barely a gameline at all to begin with.<br /> <br /> It consisted of three books total, one of which was a LARP book that compiled information from the first two books. At the absolute most, Mummy had five books if we're going to count World of Darkness: Mummy and the Mummy book for Vampire: The Masquerade 1e.<br /> <br /> Mage makes the most sense given it's the third heavy-hitter, followed by Wraith given that gameline's popularity among the &quot;True Art Personal Horror&quot; crowd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T16:26:47-08:00","id":1530410,"title":"","content":"I even agree with the mage issue, but I just wonder how they're going to deal with it, because obviously they're not very willing to deal with anything too problematic, so I wonder how they would approach the traditions, because I find it difficult for them don't cut at least one, because half of them are a bit shabby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T16:50:55-08:00","id":1530411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530410#post1530410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I even agree with the mage issue, but I just wonder how they're going to deal with it, because obviously they're not very willing to deal with anything too problematic, so I wonder how they would approach the traditions, because I find it difficult for them don't cut at least one, because half of them are a bit shabby.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a personal pet theory about M5 where the Hollow Ones and Verbena would be treated as super-duper heckin' heroic while the Celestial Chorus would get the Cult of Fenris treatment and turned into the new super-duper evil fascist Big Bad Guy, and most of the other main Traditions would be heavily sanitized and genericized. Powers would be nerfed to where Mages would be more like glorified Sorcerers and the Umbra would be cut off completely. You thought the Avatar Storm in Revised was bad? M5 would take that one step even further to ensure things remain &quot;Street Level True Art Personal Horror&quot;<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would either get sidelined into irrelevance like the Sabbat and Black Spiral Dancers did, or they'd become a cartoonish walking political strawman<br /> <br /> If we factor in the Disparate Alliance of M20, add the Sisters of Hippolyta in with the same camp as the Verbena and Hollow Ones and then add the Knights Templar in the same camp as the Celestial Chorus. I know M20 counts the Hollow Ones as part of the Disparate Alliance but let's be real, the Hollow Ones were the only one of the disparate Crafts to get a major focus from the very beginning so I kinda consider them their own thing for the purposes of this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T02:11:37-08:00","id":1530424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530411#post1530411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a personal pet theory about M5 where the Hollow Ones and Verbena would be treated as super-duper heckin' heroic while the Celestial Chorus would get the Cult of Fenris treatment and turned into the new super-duper evil fascist Big Bad Guy, and most of the other main Traditions would be heavily sanitized and genericized. Powers would be nerfed to where Mages would be more like glorified Sorcerers and the Umbra would be cut off completely. You thought the Avatar Storm in Revised was bad? M5 would take that one step even further to ensure things remain &quot;Street Level True Art Personal Horror&quot;<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would either get sidelined into irrelevance like the Sabbat and Black Spiral Dancers did, or they'd become a cartoonish walking political strawman<br /> <br /> If we factor in the Disparate Alliance of M20, add the Sisters of Hippolyta in with the same camp as the Verbena and Hollow Ones and then add the Knights Templar in the same camp as the Celestial Chorus. I know M20 counts the Hollow Ones as part of the Disparate Alliance but let's be real, the Hollow Ones were the only one of the disparate Crafts to get a major focus from the very beginning so I kinda consider them their own thing for the purposes of this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>More likely the Templars become the SI of MtA, so to speak, and the Celestial Chorus could become the faction of Mother Russia, but with another name obviously. I don't know about technocracy anymore, because unlike Sabbat and BSD they are less exaggerated and brutal villains so maybe they will have a bigger role, even if cartoonish.<br /> <br /> By the way, a question, I understand the Hollow Ones, but what about the Verbenna? What exactly would they be like as heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T07:58:56-08:00","id":1530442,"title":"","content":"I really like what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> has introduced in the other thread, the idea of Localized Consensus.<br /> <br /> With the Technocracy all but winning the Ascension War, they tried to advance the Time tables too much, and Paradox broke out so badly that Consensus broke badly.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bReality Is cracking and Marauders are awakening spontaneously.<br /> <br /> Chaos and suffering empower Nephandi, and Technocrats are increasingly divided betwern those who think Earth Is fucked and those who are fighting to save the day. They are a powerful but crumbling and besieged Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Traditions are there, trying to fix local consensus in order t\u00f2 make Reality stable, if more Dynamic, again. A bit like Anarch in V5, they are a Motley of rebels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T08:52:57-08:00","id":1530453,"title":"","content":"Hunter, Mummy, and Demon were what I'd call \u201clatter day\u201d gamelines, in that each of them spun out of the Week of Nightmares/Sixth Great Maelstrom metaplot elements that took a sledgehammer to the status quo and sent it careening off in a new direction. X5 doesn't have that, and H5 as a result is drastically different from HtR to the point that they're effectively different games. <br /> <br /> I would expect Mummy5 to do something similar, with mummies being more like the ones from the first and second editions of WoD's Mummy. None of the MtR stuff about a new Spell of Life that grafts a portion of an ancient mummy's soul into a recently deceased mortal; just the latest iteration of the mummy's cycle of death and rebirth. <br /> <br /> That said, a number of innovations that MtR made could still make their way into Mum5, such as giving them a series of splats based on which part of the soul is strongest. That, combined with the fact that Mum2 had Memory as one of its Virtues (something that I'd recommend Mum5 doing as well) would likely invite comparisons between Mum5 and CoD's Mummy: the Curse; though unlike similar criticisms of Vampire, Hunter, and Werewolf borrowing concepts from their CoD counterparts, this one would be firmly rooted in existing WoD material. <br /> <br /> D5 would likewise abandon the Latter-day plot of the walls of the Abyss being cracked by the Sixth Great Maelstrom; though I think most of DtF's setup could be salvaged: just replace the explanation given in DtF with something more like what's found in <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</b>the Dark Ages supplement Devil's Due.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T10:01:21-08:00","id":1530458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530424#post1530424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More likely the Templars become the SI of MtA, so to speak, and the Celestial Chorus could become the faction of Mother Russia, but with another name obviously. I don't know about technocracy anymore, because unlike Sabbat and BSD they are less exaggerated and brutal villains so maybe they will have a bigger role, even if cartoonish.<br /> <br /> By the way, a question, I understand the Hollow Ones, but what about the Verbenna? What exactly would they be like as heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine an M5 version of the Verbena would basically become the &quot;Sisters of Hippolyta Lite&quot; and the Wiccan elements would be emphasized above all else, even as the other Traditions become overly sanitized and genericized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T14:18:08-08:00","id":1530480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530458#post1530458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd imagine an M5 version of the Verbena would basically become the &quot;Sisters of Hippolyta Lite&quot; and the Wiccan elements would be emphasized above all else, even as the other Traditions become overly sanitized and genericized.</div> </div> </div> </div>5e splats are not overly sanitized, they are still quite full of shit, both in V5 and in W5 (lots of Tribe archetypes are monstrous), so I don't really see Traditions losing their rough edges.<br /> <br /> The trend of divorcing them from cultural origins Is instead something I see as really difficult - and by the way, I would gladly dispose of It, in the context of Mage.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-10-2024, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T14:29:24-08:00","id":1530482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530458#post1530458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd imagine an M5 version of the Verbena would basically become the &quot;Sisters of Hippolyta Lite&quot; and the Wiccan elements would be emphasized above all else, even as the other Traditions become overly sanitized and genericized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think putting a Wiccan theme goes against generalizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T14:38:46-08:00","id":1530483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530480#post1530480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5e splats are not overly sanitized, they are still quite full of shit, both in V5 and in W5 (lots of Tribe archetypes are monstrous), so I don't really see Traditions losing their rough edges.<br /> <br /> The trend of divorcing them from cultural origins Is instead something I see as really difficult - and by the way, I would gladly dispose of It, in the context of Mage.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's that idea that when you put a very exaggerated character, people just accept it and don't take it seriously, especially in the case of W5, which doesn't even sell them as heroes or anything close to that. That's not even a complaint because it could actually work.<br /> <br /> One question, when you say about removing cultural elements, are you for or against this in the case of the M5? It wasn't clear to me.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T14:54:41-08:00","id":1530485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530483#post1530483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's that idea that when you put a very exaggerated character, people just accept it and don't take it seriously, especially in the case of W5, which doesn't even sell them as heroes or anything close to that. That's not even a complaint because it could actually work.<br /> <br /> One question, when you say about removing cultural elements, are you for or against this in the case of the M5? It wasn't clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally liked what they did with Tribes in W5, sure they Need some more fleshing out to stand as autonomous rebooted Tribes<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> I'm open to solutions, but I think It would be quite difficult to maintain Paradigms without cultural elements, so I'm against cutting all ties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:38:30-08:00","id":1530496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530482#post1530482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think putting a Wiccan theme goes against generalizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wicca is explicitly something that emerged from the 20th Century Anglosphere, so there'd be far less concerns from Parawolf about cultural appropriation regarding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 02-10-2024, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:59:29-07:00","id":1533530,"title":"","content":"One thing that came to mind is that in the case of Changeling, how would they approach banality. It has already been mentioned that some members of the autumnal people are psychoanalysts or something along those lines who try to &quot;help&quot; the changelings by making them believe that this fairy side is just in their heads, consequently killing that part. Due to the possible controversy this would bring, how do you think this would be addressed in a possible fifth edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T13:55:41-07:00","id":1533534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1533530#post1533530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that came to mind is that in the case of Changeling, how would they approach banality. It has already been mentioned that some members of the autumnal people are psychoanalysts or something along those lines who try to &quot;help&quot; the changelings by making them believe that this fairy side is just in their heads, consequently killing that part. Due to the possible controversy this would bring, how do you think this would be addressed in a possible fifth edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>C20 re-approached that by casting the Autumn People as the Autism Speaks lot and religious zealots trying to torture people out of being non-straight or cis. Depending on whatever axes the people up top have to grind against C:tD, that may or may not stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T13:24:06-07:00","id":1533572,"title":"","content":"There is enough criticism of psychiatry from <i>within psychiatry</i> that Changeling could work with it if they wanted--medicalizing people who don't really fit in with society hasn't stopped entirely and isn't limited to religious zealots and NGOs. I don't think they will (for the same reasons a lot of people have trouble applying the same criticisms of science-as-practice and science-as-an-institution that I see from within the scientific community to Mage), but they could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 04-04-2024, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T13:52:59-07:00","id":1533573,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I don't see Changeling getting the X5 treatment.<br /> <br /> The only games I can see getting X5 editions that haven't already been adapted are Wraith, Mage, and Demon.<br /> <br /> Wraith is the most likely due to it being the one that's the most friendly to &quot;Street Level True Art Personal Horror&quot; of all the original games and there's the whole &quot;Street Level Renegades vs. The Hierarchy&quot; conflict.<br /> <br /> Mage is the second most likely due to the fact it's the third-most popular of the Classic WoD games and Parawolf could finally complete the &quot;Big Three&quot;.<br /> <br /> Demon is the third-most likely, and it'll largely be just because of the opportunity for Parawolf to play the whole &quot;Lucifer is good, God is evil&quot; angle completely unironically and without any of the nuance that the original gameline had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T22:19:30-07:00","id":1534541,"title":"","content":"To be honest, Vampire 5 seemed quite good. Vampires are presented as too weak, but I did not really mind many of the setting developments. On the other hand, Hunter 5 felt uninteresting, and Werewolf 5 was of low quality. I am scared that Mage 5 would be stripped of the elements that rendered it unique and would have what little genuine occult content that it had taken away. I still kind of want to see Mage 5, though. I think that it would just be surreal to see a new edition of Ascension in the contemporary world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T01:14:22-07:00","id":1537853,"title":"","content":"My post disappeared.<br /> Or maybe I imagined posting it.<br /> Or maybe it was moderated into oblivion without warning.<br /> Maybe it was the bit about my theory on 'exoticization' not being inherently bad and actually being a component of creative process, due to a lot of stories being spurned by such kind of dreams. To be clear I was talking about CtD.<br /> Or it was the bit on the flat-earthers, conspiracies and MtA.<br /> Or it was something else that I don't remember.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to make it shorter than before:<br /> <br /> 1) Aside from the Traditions depiction, MtA can be seen as problematic because the premise of the game can be perceived as a whole big conspiracy theory being true. I won't try to hint again at why it can be problematic in our times. But if we take that from MtA, we basically take away the whole point of it.<br /> <br /> 2) Changeling is too hard to sell.<br /> Either it's too hopeful and dreamy, and so doesn't fit WOD5 which goes hard on the dark and gloom and brooding. Or it can become the truly more depressing one, because it sort of forces roleplayers to look at themselves and how they see and live their whole 'imaginary worlds' passion.<br /> Also it's a 'high concept' game. But to be 'high concept', you have to make hard statements about things.<br /> For example to conside going to your mundane job every day a total drag, an absolutely Banal thing, and by Changeling POV basically a torture.<br /> It is not a mature thing to say, it is not necessarily the opinion of the writers of the game, but it is part of the point.<br /> If you make hard statements someone can be offended, there is no way around it.<br /> I don't think it's going to happen unless they discard the whole concept and do their own thing. Changeling the Lost was a good game, so I'd suggest to take a similar route and make their own thing, instead of sullying someone else's creation.<br /> <br /> 3) Wraith is probably the easier one. While it's not really a game of &quot;Street Level True Art Personal Horror&quot;, or at least it's not fully committed to it, much like Vampire it can be taken partially as it is and made like that just like V5. The transition is easier. Because while there are multidimensional overarching or world ending plots like in VtM, there is also the niche of &quot;anarchs against the Man at street level and we do our own thing in our turf&quot; side of things. It is indeed the more similar to VtM, because in the other three games the world-scale concept and theme is too much part of the game/setting itself.<br /> <br /> I'll add that I wouldn't mind a Mummy game mixing stuff between the old mummies and Mummy the Curse to make their own thing, with something like Doom Dice that makes you go wrath of the gods mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T14:43:31-07:00","id":1537905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537853#post1537853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My post disappeared.<br /> Or maybe I imagined posting it.<br /> Or maybe it was moderated into oblivion without warning.<br /> Maybe it was the bit about my theory on 'exoticization' not being inherently bad and actually being a component of creative process, due to a lot of stories being spurned by such kind of dreams. To be clear I was talking about CtD.<br /> Or it was the bit on the flat-earthers, conspiracies and MtA.<br /> Or it was something else that I don't remember.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to make it shorter than before:<br /> <br /> 1) Aside from the Traditions depiction, MtA can be seen as problematic because the premise of the game can be perceived as a whole big conspiracy theory being true. I won't try to hint again at why it can be problematic in our times. But if we take that from MtA, we basically take away the whole point of it.<br /> <br /> 2) Changeling is too hard to sell.<br /> Either it's too hopeful and dreamy, and so doesn't fit WOD5 which goes hard on the dark and gloom and brooding. Or it can become the truly more depressing one, because it sort of forces roleplayers to look at themselves and how they see and live their whole 'imaginary worlds' passion.<br /> Also it's a 'high concept' game. But to be 'high concept', you have to make hard statements about things.<br /> For example to conside going to your mundane job every day a total drag, an absolutely Banal thing, and by Changeling POV basically a torture.<br /> It is not a mature thing to say, it is not necessarily the opinion of the writers of the game, but it is part of the point.<br /> If you make hard statements someone can be offended, there is no way around it.<br /> I don't think it's going to happen unless they discard the whole concept and do their own thing. Changeling the Lost was a good game, so I'd suggest to take a similar route and make their own thing, instead of sullying someone else's creation.<br /> <br /> 3) Wraith is probably the easier one. While it's not really a game of &quot;Street Level True Art Personal Horror&quot;, or at least it's not fully committed to it, much like Vampire it can be taken partially as it is and made like that just like V5. The transition is easier. Because while there are multidimensional overarching or world ending plots like in VtM, there is also the niche of &quot;anarchs against the Man at street level and we do our own thing in our turf&quot; side of things. It is indeed the more similar to VtM, because in the other three games the world-scale concept and theme is too much part of the game/setting itself.<br /> <br /> I'll add that I wouldn't mind a Mummy game mixing stuff between the old mummies and Mummy the Curse to make their own thing, with something like Doom Dice that makes you go wrath of the gods mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Changeling is a no-go for Parawolf for all of the reasons you outlined.<br /> <br /> Wraith and Mage are strong contenders for the next victim of Parawolf's patented X5 Hackjob, the former due to thematics and the latter due to popularity <br /> <br /> But I also think Demon is a dark horse contender for the next X5 game and is more likely than one would expect. If we get a D5, expect it to be on par with something akin to &quot;The Last Resurrection&quot; or a Satanic Temple equivalent of a Pureflix movie. The Reconcilers will definitely be given the same shameful treatment that the Get of Fenris got in W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T16:08:08-07:00","id":1537909,"title":"","content":"Actually, they could satisfy their hunger for gritty, street-level operations and character assassinations of splats in Changeling by having the sidhe suffer from King Ironheart's Madness or something and make them all start terrorizing the commoners in a kind of Accordance War 2.0, or just copying Vampire's setup completely with a veneer of Changeling, complete with giving Autumn People a place in the 2nd Inquisition.<br /> <br /> I still contend that Demon came around far too late for any of the internal crew at ParaWolf to care about it that much. If you're fixated on details from player's guide and splatbooks from 1993-1995, you probably don't care what they did in 2002-2004. Revised also seems like a dirty word to them. So, either they ignore it, or they do to it what they did to H:tR and knock it back to being about a completely different set of characters with no relation to the Elohim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T16:30:06-07:00","id":1537910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537909#post1537909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they could satisfy their hunger for gritty, street-level operations and character assassinations of splats in Changeling by having the sidhe suffer from King Ironheart's Madness or something and make them all start terrorizing the commoners in a kind of Accordance War 2.0, or just copying Vampire's setup completely with a veneer of Changeling, complete with giving Autumn People a place in the 2nd Inquisition.<br /> <br /> I still contend that Demon came around far too late for any of the internal crew at ParaWolf to care about it that much. If you're fixated on details from player's guide and splatbooks from 1993-1995, you probably don't care what they did in 2002-2004. Revised also seems like a dirty word to them. So, either they ignore it, or they do to it what they did to H:tR and knock it back to being about a completely different set of characters with no relation to the Elohim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, you do have a point where they could do a C5 Hackjob by giving Sidhe a treatment that's like halfway between what the Camarilla and Get of Fenris got.<br /> <br /> As for Demon, the Parawolf crew cares a lot about Classic 90's era WoD while also hating it to an extreme degree (even if it's in a passive-aggressive sort of way) and tbh, V5's decision to kinda-sorta update the metaplot and drastically change several clans (even renaming a few of them while also turning them into twisted mockeries of themselves) was an early red flag for me.<br /> <br /> While the earliest V5 guys aren't there anymore, they set a precedent that Parawolf used as a springboard to go even further off the deep end with H5 and W5 and later V5 releases.<br /> <br /> Their own seeming indifference to the Revised years might not apply to Demon, given the fact that a lot of the Parawolf guys have very blatant specific political agendas and are very unsubtle about it. You are right that H5 was more of a hackjob treatment for The Hunters Hunted/Year of the Hunter than for Reckoning itself, but there's a very specific reason why I think Demon might be a dark horse contender for the next X5 game alongside the far more obvious Mage 5 and Wraith 5.<br /> <br /> Demon is a game where you literally play as fallen angels, Lucifer/Satan is literally depicted as a hero, and God is both absent and kinda portrayed in a very negative light. Now, there was more nuance to it than that, but Parawolf probably doesn't care about that and only zeroes in on &quot;You're street-level punk demons fighting against the ultimate incarnation of The Man!&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, I can see Demon getting a W5-esque treatment where The Reconcilers are given the worst Cult of Fenris-tier strawman treatment, acting like a bizarre mix of medieval crusaders, Jack Chick-tier Evangelical fundamentalists, and 17th Century Puritans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T17:58:44-07:00","id":1537917,"title":"","content":"I honestly think there's just no less or more likely contender except by how much they think their vision of Vampire demands/accommodates a given splat.<br /> <br /> Hunter coming second took everyone by surprise when announced, but it was there because of course, Vampires are targeted by hunters so this splat desperately needs to exist.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is less needed, but it's still the most traditional enemy for Vampires in WoD. I think Mage is the next one, if done at all, but after that it's all a matter of what they want to put next as a foil to Vampires.<br /> <br /> And the W5 treatment makes it clear that the divergence between those lines and their &quot;Street-Level 'punk'&quot; is a moot point: they'll simply hack the lines until they become what they want, previous editions be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:05:42-07:00","id":1537918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537917#post1537917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think there's just no less or more likely contender except by how much they think their vision of Vampire demands/accommodates a given splat.<br /> <br /> Hunter coming second took everyone by surprise when announced, but it was there because of course, Vampires are targeted by hunters so this splat desperately needs to exist.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is less needed, but it's still the most traditional enemy for Vampires in WoD. I think Mage is the next one, if done at all, but after that it's all a matter of what they want to put next as a foil to Vampires.<br /> <br /> And the W5 treatment makes it clear that the divergence between those lines and their &quot;Street-Level 'punk'&quot; is a moot point: they'll simply hack the lines until they become what they want, previous editions be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tbh, Mage probably is the most likely of all games to get the X5 treatment due to both it being the third most popular of the WoD games and the fact they'll complete the trio of &quot;Vampire, Werewolf, and Witch&quot; too. <br /> <br /> If I were to rank the likelihood of the games getting a 5th Edition from most likely to least likely, I'd say that Mage is the most likely, Wraith and Demon are in a very close second and third, Changeling is a very distant fourth, and Mummy ain't gonna happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:34:36-07:00","id":1537921,"title":"","content":"I'd say there's a chance for mummy to happen because it's originally a Vampire supplement. It had indeed two whole editions as a Vampire companion splat of sorts before the third where it became its own line.<br /> <br /> Not saying it's a particularly high chance. But it's there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:42:29-07:00","id":1537924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537921#post1537921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's a chance for mummy to happen because it's originally a Vampire supplement. It had indeed two whole editions as a Vampire companion splat of sorts before the third where it became its own line.<br /> <br /> Not saying it's a particularly high chance. But it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, as H5 feels more like a defilement of The Hunters Hunted (a Vampire supplement) than a defilement of Hunter: The Reckoning itself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:59:38-07:00","id":1537926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537917#post1537917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the W5 treatment makes it clear that the divergence between those lines and their &quot;Street-Level 'punk'&quot; is a moot point: they'll simply hack the lines until they become what they want, previous editions be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've said before that I expect M5 to take heavy cues from Unknown Armies. Which wouldn't necessarily make for a bad game, but 1) people want to play Mage for the ideas Mage brings and 2) UA3 isn't that old, those of us interested in it's ideas likely own it.<br /> <br /> I really like comparing UA3 to WoD5, because both make an attempt to focus the games on street level play. But UA3 played heavily into existing elements of the game: it's occult organizations were already small, obsession was a constant theme from first edition, and power always had a price. While there's some setting elements that have been pushed aside there's still acknowledgement that they exist and I get a feeling of 'this will come back if a writer is interested enough to make it work. Meanwhile WoD5 feels like it's carving large chunks out of the setting because it didn't fit one person's views.<br /> <br /> I suspect M5 might have had trouble getting off the ground when they tried to make the Technocracy into TNI, and failed to realise why the two organizations vary so much, alongside with a difficulty in downplaying all the nonwestern cultural ties. Neither are issues that can't be solved via a hatchet, but I wouldn't be shocked if they're really struggling with groups like the Akashic Brotherhood and Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> But my money is still on M5 being next. Maybe C5 if they just decide to turn it into CtL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T19:27:11-07:00","id":1537929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537926#post1537926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I've said before that I expect M5 to take heavy cues from Unknown Armies. Which wouldn't necessarily make for a bad game, but 1) people want to play Mage for the ideas Mage brings and 2) UA3 isn't that old, those of us interested in it's ideas likely own it.<br /> <br /> I really like comparing UA3 to WoD5, because both make an attempt to focus the games on street level play. But UA3 played heavily into existing elements of the game: it's occult organizations were already small, obsession was a constant theme from first edition, and power always had a price. While there's some setting elements that have been pushed aside there's still acknowledgement that they exist and I get a feeling of 'this will come back if a writer is interested enough to make it work. Meanwhile WoD5 feels like it's carving large chunks out of the setting because it didn't fit one person's views.<br /> <br /> I suspect M5 might have had trouble getting off the ground when they tried to make the Technocracy into TNI, and failed to realise why the two organizations vary so much, alongside with a difficulty in downplaying all the nonwestern cultural ties. Neither are issues that can't be solved via a hatchet, but I wouldn't be shocked if they're really struggling with groups like the Akashic Brotherhood and Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> But my money is still on M5 being next. <b>Maybe C5 if they just decide to turn it into CtL</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could make the sidhe work like the Tzimisce, picking up random humans to magically mutilate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T02:05:50-07:00","id":1537989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537910#post1537910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon is a game where you literally play as fallen angels, Lucifer/Satan is literally depicted as a hero, and God is both absent and kinda portrayed in a very negative light. Now, there was more nuance to it than that, but Parawolf probably doesn't care about that and only zeroes in on &quot;You're street-level punk demons fighting against the ultimate incarnation of The Man!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see much affection from WoD5 developers towards the 'fight the Man' idea, at the end of the day (look at the Beckoning or the 'accruing capital' thing).<br /> Fight the Man was, in a way or the other, part of the premise of all the original splats anyway.<br /> They didn't look so Punk when I was younger and I began with revised, but in retrospective they were.<br /> From a middle class perspective, of course. But that's where edgy literature usually comes from.<br /> <br /> I never thought God in DtF could be seen as the ultimate 'The Man', but you're right. It was there. And I would totally play DtF like that lol. Fight the Man.<br /> <br /> But a D5 wouldn't be like that.<br /> Taking the monotheistic and Lucifer stuff as in 'the bible is right, sorta' would be seen as cultural narrowing.<br /> If you take a look at reddit when they talk about DtF you'll see that it's something not liked much anymore.<br /> The majority would prefer generic critter that is called Demon for simplicity but can be applied to any kind of creation myth or malevolent entity. I'm not against such a thing, I just think it would be a different game experience.<br /> <br /> My take is that the original DtF is not really that different from making a game centered on descendants of greek myths, aside from the edgy factor of teenage rebellion against a religion that is traditionally rather repressive about preferences and life choices.<br /> But my take doesn't matter. I'm not the Technocracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T03:07:49-07:00","id":1537991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537989#post1537989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But my take doesn't matter. I'm not the Technocracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Only the antidiluvian they supposedly shot down kkkk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T07:47:10-07:00","id":1537997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1537991#post1537991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only the antidiluvian they supposedly shot down kkkk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see the illusion still stands!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T08:18:30-07:00","id":1543681,"title":"","content":"I'm getting a lot of confusing news.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm seeing articles about Paradox's new CEO is fed up with Parawolf and viewing Bloodlines 2 as a dead end, but on the other hand, I've also heard rumors of Mage 5th being close in the pipeline and Renegade announcing three new supplements for V5, H5, and W5.<br /> <br /> What is going on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T08:28:39-07:00","id":1543684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1543681#post1543681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting a lot of confusing news.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm seeing articles about Paradox's new CEO is fed up with Parawolf and viewing Bloodlines 2 as a dead end, but on the other hand, I've also heard rumors of Mage 5th being close in the pipeline and Renegade announcing three new supplements for V5, H5, and W5.<br /> <br /> What is going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>The licensees are working independently of the main branch and will probably continue on until the lights go out. Much like how Onyx Path was originally slated to release a new version of V:tM as its 4th edition, but then CCP sold the license to PDX...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T09:56:12-07:00","id":1543687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1543681#post1543681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting a lot of confusing news.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm seeing articles about Paradox's new CEO is fed up with Parawolf and viewing Bloodlines 2 as a dead end, but on the other hand, I've also heard rumors of Mage 5th being close in the pipeline and Renegade announcing three new supplements for V5, H5, and W5.<br /> <br /> What is going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox holds the WOD-license.<br /> <br /> Renegade is a separate company that is responsible for the supplements. So with Renegade, we know what's going on and at their recent RenegadeCon they announced the next three supplements for V5, H5 and W5 (I made <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1543591-renegade-con-oct-2024-upcoming-wod5e-books#post1543591\">a thread</a> for these announcements).<br /> <br /> But there's also a WOD-team directly working for Paradox who supposedly are working on the next corebook. But we know nothing concrete about when the next corebook will be released. Justin Achilli mentioned writing down some ideas for a potential M5 - but he left. To add more confusion, the new WOD-lead-developer isn't part of this team (like Justin Achilli was) but rather works for Renegade. So who even knows what's going on here...<br /> <br /> But Paradox is a video-game-company and that's where their main-focus is. And yet, Bloodlines 2 which was supposed to be their flagship-title has turned into this giant headache for them. Development-hell, delays, changes in expectations... Clearly they aren't happy with how things have turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T10:17:45-07:00","id":1543690,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AKMzMZWRKVc\" target=\"_blank\">A dramatization of Paradox on acquiring the WoD license, before and after.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T14:45:57-07:00","id":1543704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1543681#post1543681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting a lot of confusing news.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm seeing articles about Paradox's new CEO is fed up with Parawolf and viewing Bloodlines 2 as a dead end, but on the other hand, I've also heard rumors of Mage 5th being close in the pipeline and Renegade announcing three new supplements for V5, H5, and W5.<br /> <br /> What is going on?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this would have anything to do with it since they are different branches of entertainment, but I heard that some companies with licenses to produce films from certain franchises have to use them from time to time in order not to lose the license. Wouldn't that be something like that?I don't know if this would have anything to do with it since they are different branches of entertainment, but I heard that some companies with licenses to produce films from certain franchises have to use them from time to time in order not to lose the license. Wouldn't that be something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T16:08:43-07:00","id":1543712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1543681#post1543681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm seeing articles about Paradox's new CEO is fed up with Parawolf and viewing Bloodlines 2 as a dead end</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the fact that BL2 is just one piece of the puzzle, there's the fact that IIRC they don't have a new CEO, just a placeholder for the actual one who\u2019s on leave. The guy who\u2019s really into being WoD\u2019s owner is still the one calling the shots.<br /> <br /> Other than that, those aren\u2019t as strictly related things as it seems, even if it wasn\u2019t a license to Renegade. The company won\u2019t stop working on the IP they have to make money, even if small change for their size, just because they don\u2019t want it anymore. That would be to just waste money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T09:16:44-07:00","id":1544465,"title":"","content":"From the looks of it? Curseborne. <br /> <br /> What line of thought led them to believe anyone is gonna touch that with a 10-foot pole after the killing of CofD &amp; the gutting of WoD is anyone's guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T13:07:09-07:00","id":1544488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1544465#post1544465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the looks of it? Curseborne.<br /> <br /> What line of thought led them to believe anyone is gonna touch that with a 10-foot pole after the killing of CofD &amp; the gutting of WoD is anyone's guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can work as much as anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T13:32:31-07:00","id":1544492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1544465#post1544465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the looks of it? Curseborne.<br /> <br /> What line of thought led them to believe anyone is gonna touch that with a 10-foot pole after the killing of CofD &amp; the gutting of WoD is anyone's guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, OPP weren't the ones responsible. They just got the door shut on them after doing celebrated work on the IPs for a decade, with people on hand who had been working on the IPs since the IPs existed. So while the sun shines, they'll make hay. Or ergot while in the dark, I'm not sure which one is more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T17:54:33-07:00","id":1544523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1544465#post1544465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the looks of it? Curseborne.<br /> <br /> What line of thought led them to believe anyone is gonna touch that with a 10-foot pole after the killing of CofD &amp; the gutting of WoD is anyone's guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curseborne seems to be OPP making lemonade after whatever's going on with CofD seemingly ending. It's possible that OPP threw in the towel on CofD, but considering the big holes in some lines, particularly Deviant, I find that unlikely.<br /> <br /> Which is important to note: Curseborne is OPP, WoD5 is Paradox. CofD is owned by Paradox but at this point is pretty associated with OPP.<br /> <br /> Now to be fair you are under no obligation to buy or like Curseborne, but it's pretty irrelevant to WoD5 outside of being a competitor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T13:14:21-07:00","id":1544865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1530390#post1530390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not. We've had this a couple of times already and it's just a good way to get people's bile up. Let it go, it will be what it will be. Vote with your waller and play what you enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the then White Wolf decided to nuke the World of Darkness with their &quot;end of the world&quot; so that they could sell their &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;, current &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot;, I decided I would never, ever for the rest of my life ever spend a single coin at anything &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;. I stick to my decision, and thus I'll never ever buy anything related to Chronicles of Darkness, as a matter of principle. And I say, CofD is a pretty good setting. But because of the way they treated me as a client, they lost me forever, and I just simply don't care what they do afterwards.<br /> <br /> I also hate everything WOD5 related, but at least they had the decency to not demand me to thrown everything prior into the garbage and buy their new stuff.<br /> <br /> If indeed, they do keep the &quot;Legacy World of Darkness&quot; and turn this new soft reboot/alternative thing which is WoD5 into something good, I might give it a spin because of that, because they are not treating me like a clown when they did more than 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> As of right now however, I have absolutely zero interest about anything related to this new &quot;edition&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T06:17:58-07:00","id":1544885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1544865#post1544865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When the then White Wolf decided to nuke the World of Darkness with their &quot;end of the world&quot; so that they could sell their &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;, current &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot;, I decided I would never, ever for the rest of my life ever spend a single coin at anything &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;. I stick to my decision, and thus I'll never ever buy anything related to Chronicles of Darkness, as a matter of principle. And I say, CofD is a pretty good setting. But because of the way they treated me as a client, they lost me forever, and I just simply don't care what they do afterwards.<br /> <br /> I also hate everything WOD5 related, but at least they had the decency to not demand me to thrown everything prior into the garbage and buy their new stuff.<br /> <br /> If indeed, they do keep the &quot;Legacy World of Darkness&quot; and turn this new soft reboot/alternative thing which is WoD5 into something good, I might give it a spin because of that, because they are not treating me like a clown when they did more than 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> As of right now however, I have absolutely zero interest about anything related to this new &quot;edition&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Early oughties WW didn't know that their experiment with Terra Verde would have led to a successful, if comparatively meager, continuation of their business without the need for warehouse space. And Terra Verde only launched after the setting that was written as being an apocalyptic hot mess on the brink of destruction ended with the logical conclusions of five years of &quot;These are the Final Nights!&quot;<br /> <br /> As for WoD5, I think it's telling that one of the forum's foremost advocates for it eventually decided that it wasn't working out after all. I've seen the turnaround that was Shadowrun Sixth World Edition going from a terrible mess at launch to today's functional, trim, and clean-cut edition of choice for many. But the books lining up for WoD5? They don't seem to be that. Shattered Nation, indeed, seems to just be digging the hole deeper. And they are absolutely treating fans of the prior releases of the WoD as clowns; the entire operation is being run by a One True Wayist Vampire LARP main, so if you have a play style that doesn't line up with what's in the books, they're telling you that they don't want you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T08:00:47-07:00","id":1544889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1544885#post1544885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Early oughties WW didn't know that their experiment with Terra Verde would have led to a successful, if comparatively meager, continuation of their business without the need for warehouse space. And Terra Verde only launched after the setting that was written as being an apocalyptic hot mess on the brink of destruction ended with the logical conclusions of five years of &quot;These are the Final Nights!&quot;<br /> <br /> As for WoD5, I think it's telling that one of the forum's foremost advocates for it eventually decided that it wasn't working out after all. I've seen the turnaround that was Shadowrun Sixth World Edition going from a terrible mess at launch to today's functional, trim, and clean-cut edition of choice for many. But the books lining up for WoD5? They don't seem to be that. Shattered Nation, indeed, seems to just be digging the hole deeper. And they are absolutely treating fans of the prior releases of the WoD as clowns; the entire operation is being run by a One True Wayist Vampire LARP main, so if you have a play style that doesn't line up with what's in the books, they're telling you that they don't want you there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not untrue. My point was simply that if they keep a line of &quot;Legacy WoD&quot;, separating what we all love from... Whatever that WoD5 is... AND (and this a big &quot;and&quot;) they massively improve things in the far far future, then I could buy the stuff.<br /> <br /> Im not holding my breath on the minimal chances of either of those ever happening thou<br /> <br /> Edit: yeah, Shattered Nation, from what I peaked out briefly, is just simply awful. I wouldn't touch it with a 100 light-years pole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 10-28-2024, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:35:06-07:00","id":1544919,"title":"","content":"One shudders to imagine what they have planned afterward. Or how M5 is going to end up. If there was a betting pool, the categories would be something like &quot;All mages are now linear sorcerers&quot;, &quot;The Technocracy rolled back to 1e and then got worse&quot;, &quot;You will have a Quiet counter that permanently takes your character out at 5, and/or another stat that does the same at 5, and you will not be able to decrease them, only transfer them back and forth, unless you find a rare item in the Umbra&quot;, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T20:39:15-07:00","id":1545034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1530389-future-wod5-titles?p=1544919#post1544919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One shudders to imagine what they have planned afterward. Or how M5 is going to end up. If there was a betting pool, the categories would be something like &quot;All mages are now linear sorcerers&quot;, &quot;The Technocracy rolled back to 1e and then got worse&quot;, &quot;You will have a Quiet counter that permanently takes your character out at 5, and/or another stat that does the same at 5, and you will not be able to decrease them, only transfer them back and forth, unless you find a rare item in the Umbra&quot;, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much around that. It wouldn't surprise me.<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no expectations towards M5 and yet I'm sure I'll still be disappointed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}